          "text": "d) Temperature: 1 cold\n\ne) Humidity: 2 - humid\n\nf) Wind: none\n\ng) Post~: Relative. 1/0~3ERVADOR\n   a- Distance: between 0 and observer,                                     L ::l..   over the ground: Not possible to calculate,\n       at a great altitude.\n\nb) It started its movement at 45 degrees.\n\n8. Location: Habited - Urban -\n   d) Various people scattered between others in a group - the main problem of the city\n\n9. Presence in media: Houses - factories - schools - television receivers - electric power substations - electrical appliances (in) , lines of high and low voltage, transformers, highways - water pipelines.\n\n13. Situation of the observation at the moment of the sighting:\n\n      a - observer ... saw a light (the main light of the city).\n      Observation made with the naked eye\n                              - - -- DA:)03 RE ':\"\"RE ';: ~ AO 0 NI.\n\n1- Description: Free, made by the observer\n            Appeared a light in the form of a star, with yellow light. Speed comparable to that of an airplane. Suddenly, it increased in size and changed from yellow to orange and then changed direction, following north.\n            At the moment it increased in size, it was about the size of a plate.\n            When heading north, its speed decreased. It did not stop but changed direction at that moment, appearing to the observer. It did not resemble a star. It emitted reflections. Constant light, not blinking.\n\n2- Technical data:\n\n                                        5 minutes of duration, approximately\n                                        Shape: round but with pointed ends at various moments.\n                                        Similar to a 60-rel light.\n                                        Apparent opacity:\n                                        Luminosity: constant\n                                        Color: from yellow to orange\n\n3- The movement was balanced, with a slow descent.\n\nc- Effect on the observer:\n                Speed of the object: approximately 7 KXK.%iI\n                It went north.\n                Currently, it is heading back to its last position.\n\n4- There were no noises.\n\nCollection of official documents from the Brazilian Air Force (SIOANI), converted to a digital file by Edison Boaventura Jr / GUG – Group Ufológico de Guarujá",
